==English==
===Etymology===
Jack Ketch was an excecutioner employed by King Charles II and  King James II of England.  He was died in 1686.  He is best know for his botched executions of William Russell, Lord Russell and James Scott, 1st Duke of Monmouth.  He was believed to be either very inept at his job or sadistic. 
